# Phase 2 - Auth & RBAC Test Collection

## Signup - Create Organization & First User
POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orgName": "Acme Warehouse Co",
  "orgSlug": "acme-warehouse",
  "userName": "John Owner",
  "email": "john@acme.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

###

## Login - Get Tokens
POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@acme.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "orgSlug": "acme-warehouse"
}

###

## Login - Wrong Credentials (should fail)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@acme.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword",
  "orgSlug": "acme-warehouse"
}

###

## Login - Wrong Org (should fail)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@acme.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "orgSlug": "different-org"
}

###

## Refresh Token
POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

###

## Logout
POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

###

## Test Protected Route (GET /api/products example - will add in Phase 3)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/products
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

###

## Test RBAC - Should fail if role insufficient
GET http://localhost:4000/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
